From c5002ac5f634dd24ef015ab2226fa1fdc1700a34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tad <tad.keller@pm.me>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 13:36:48 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] audio: default AIDL HAL: optional codec routing via
 mixer_paths.xml

If /vendor/etc/mixer_paths.xml (audio_route format) is present, the primary
module applies its top-level controls at startup and switches to the path
matching the connected device type when a primary stream changes device
(speaker, earpiece, headphones, builtin-mic, headset-mic). Without the file
behaviour is unchanged. Lets boards with a plain ALSA codec, such as the
Librem 5 (WM8962), use the default HAL instead of a custom one.

Change-Id: I7b69855886f8da6573702d4f40a65c0dba7adc11
---
